[{:db/id 17592186096834 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-48a4330e-b61a-5908-b482-77c947469ce8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096836 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-45517c4f-34c5-5613-91b3-714b64a55e54"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186320707 :answer-field/correct "answer-e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b" :answer/id #uuid "e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-48a4330e-b61a-5908-b482-77c947469ce8" :question/id #uuid "48a4330e-b61a-5908-b482-77c947469ce8" :question/math-academy-id "q-350842" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\,dx=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{1}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{5}]-\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}}{5}-(\\frac{{e}^{5}}{25}-\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(5{e}^{5}-{e}^{5}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(4{e}^{5}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e0c4dfe-2a2c-535e-956d-62ad8cee8229"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e0c4dfe-2a2c-535e-956d-62ad8cee8229" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e0c4dfe-2a2c-535e-956d-62ad8cee8229" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31" :answer/id #uuid "1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4e^5+1}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-45517c4f-34c5-5613-91b3-714b64a55e54" :question/id #uuid "45517c4f-34c5-5613-91b3-714b64a55e54" :question/math-academy-id "q-78972" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8afc707b-a42b-5621-ace9-e6a014a201bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8afc707b-a42b-5621-ace9-e6a014a201bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "8afc707b-a42b-5621-ace9-e6a014a201bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd63e3cd-ff82-5ade-9211-594e2bfdb08c" "answer-cc74e90b-cf7b-5156-89e6-293ad43d67ea" "answer-1fac7b1b-401e-571f-9ac1-c8035cba4079" "answer-612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" "answer-92b952c7-daa6-5ab4-a7f5-81b3cf909d3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd63e3cd-ff82-5ade-9211-594e2bfdb08c" :answer/id #uuid "bd63e3cd-ff82-5ade-9211-594e2bfdb08c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc74e90b-cf7b-5156-89e6-293ad43d67ea" :answer/id #uuid "cc74e90b-cf7b-5156-89e6-293ad43d67ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fac7b1b-401e-571f-9ac1-c8035cba4079" :answer/id #uuid "1fac7b1b-401e-571f-9ac1-c8035cba4079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" :answer/id #uuid "612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92b952c7-daa6-5ab4-a7f5-81b3cf909d3a" :answer/id #uuid "92b952c7-daa6-5ab4-a7f5-81b3cf909d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097927 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.\n$$\n\nThe method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n\n$$\n\\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe usually let $u = x,$ but that would leave us with $v' = \\ln(x)$ which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our $u$ and $v'$ slightly differently, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow the formula of integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{u}\\cdot {{x}_{⏟}}_{{v}^{′}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should *always* identify the logarithmic function with $u,$ not with $v'.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096910 :activity/expected-seconds 1320.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
